"citation_ids":["cite.long.record-257bm-c9"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-c9"],"id":"long.record-257bm-c9","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.77 (Quotients in the upper half of the index range)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.77, p. 66, label record:257bm-c9","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For integers $d\\ge2$ and $d\\le M<2d$,\n$$\nq(M,d)=\\left\\lfloor\\frac{2^M}{2^d-1}\\right\\rfloor=2^{M-d}.\n$$\nIndeed, the quotient is $2^{M-d}+2^{M-d}/(2^d-1)$, whose second term is strictly between zero and one. In Theorem 6.75, the available ranks $d=c+1,\\ldots,2c-2$ therefore supply the binary weights $2^{c-3},\\ldots,1$. They represent every integer from $0$ to $2^{c-2}-1$, which explains both the capacity bound and the choice of terminal depth.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c9","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c9","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c9%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_boolean_word_of_lt_two_pow%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c9%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.exists_boolean_word_of_lt_two_pow%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.exists_boolean_word_of_lt_two_pow"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/nodes/long.record-257bm-c9","id":"sha256:264b08973a5f23b2f98ad989b0c1708096513d86929f19048623a2a9fe18092c/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-c9%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.localMersenneQuotient_eq_